From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:18:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Optionally configure the firmware's
 power controllers

The initdata leaves the controller words of POWER_PERFORMANCE zero
apart from the sample period and the state ceiling: no utilisation
target, no gains or filters, no maximum power and no thermal enables.
macOS fills the same constants into its POWER object.

Add g16_fw_controllers (load time, default 0). When set, the initdata
writes those words the way the Gravity Linux G16 driver builds them in
g16_power.rs, evaluated for the J604: the ADT's 8 ms sample period and
turbo controller input, ten performance rows, a maximum power of 36294
mW and Gravity's defaults for the properties the J604's ADT does not
carry. The host keeps its S1 startup and then publishes 1000 in the
selectors whenever the cooling ceiling allows the top state, as with
g16_selectors=1, so that the firmware picks the state.

Each word was checked against macOS 26B123's own copy of the object at
INIT; where macOS differs from Gravity's default, macOS's value is used.

The words come from GPL-2.0-only code, so they live in a new
GPL-2.0-only file, fw/controllers.rs, which credits the Gravity Linux
contributors.

Assisted-by: LLM
