+//! The firmware's own power and performance controllers (`g16_fw_controllers`).
+//!
+//! The qualified initdata leaves the controller words of POWER_PERFORMANCE zero apart from
+//! the sample period and the state ceiling: no utilisation target, no gains, no filters, no
+//! maximum power and no thermal enables. These are the words the Gravity driver builds in the
+//! same object (its bundle offset minus 0x5380, the object Runtime +0x469 points to), with the
+//! J604's inputs: the ADT's sgx gpu-pwr-sample-period-aic-clks (200000 clocks, 8 ms) and
+//! gpu-turbo-controller-input (0, present), the J604's ten performance rows (900 for the top
+//! state, 100 for the base), a maximum power of 36294 mW (the value macOS has in Globals at
+//! INIT) and Gravity's defaults for every property the J604's ADT does not carry. Where macOS
+//! fills the same constants into the POWER object they are equal (40, 2.42, 0.135, 11000,
+//! 8000, 120.0, 9600, 300, 1.3, 625, 0.25, 1.2, 15.0, 5.0). Checked word by word against
+//! macOS 26B123's own copy of this object at INIT: where macOS differs from Gravity (the duty
+//! of the 0x21f0 block is 100, not 40) macOS's value is used. macOS's table has eleven rows
+//! (top 1000); the J604's ten rows here make the top 900, and the words derived from it
+//! follow that.
+
+/// The top state's frequency, MHz (Gravity: its eleventh row; here the J604's ceiling row).
+pub(crate) const TOP_FREQUENCY: usize = 0x21fc;
